{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778551200,"nonce":"wd0UGIyTXwSj3ZDV4swRqnlekSw=","title":"Downgrade unscoped auth:resolved events from channel event to passive log","message":"When an auth:resolved SSE event has `target_session_id = null` (legacy/unscoped), the channel server currently broadcasts it as a channel event (`notifications/claude/channel`) to every connected session. This wakes every running agent for a result none of them submitted.\n\nNow that `mandible auth request` reliably includes `target_session_id`, the broadcast path is no longer needed as a safety net. Unscoped events should be downgraded to passive logging messages (`sendLoggingMessage`) so the info is still visible on the next user prompt but does not trigger an immediate agent turn in unrelated sessions.\n\n**Current behavior** (`notifications.ts:124`):\n```typescript\nif (targetSessionId == null) {\n  deliverAuth(); // sends channel event to ALL listeners\n}\n```\n\n**Desired behavior**:\n```typescript\nif (targetSessionId == null) {\n  sendNotification(\"auth_resolved\", formatAuthResolved(data)); // passive log only\n}\n```\n\nSame change for the `ownSessionId == null` fallback branch (line 132) — if the channel server does not know its own session ID, it should also use passive logging rather than channel events.\n\nSurfaced during testing: a pre-session-tracking agent submitted auth request `05bc487f` without a session ID, and the resolved event woke an unrelated session via channel event broadcast.","files":null}]}